# Constitution

- Shared memory is the durable store when `memory_repo.path` is configured.
- Workspace `.pamem/config.toml` owns repo location, sharing mode, and sync behavior.
- `MEMORY.md` stays a thin index, not a transcript.
- Runtime startup hooks are read-only loaders; they do not repair or sync shared memory.
- Sync for the memory repo is handled only by an assigned executor through `.pamem/scripts/memory-sync.sh` or external sync tooling.
